      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T17:24:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP is used in the TC attaches, I could envision valid scenarios for it to be set to TYPEC_RP_3A0 in general (ex. honeybuns).  Would we only disallow it if a board is defining CONFIG_USB_PD_3A_PORTS \u003e 0?   \n\nI believe the route we\u0027re going so far for honeybuns is to have dpm_get_source_pdo() overridden in the board to allow it to pick power per-port, and it won\u0027t be using our source-out allocation since both ports can always source 3A (at different voltages based on port).  So it could use CONFIG_USB_PD_3A_PORTS \u003d\u003d 0, and I could add a note in the config.h definition that this disables the DPM source-out policy.",
      "parentUuid": "df4ff87f_9a2581af",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 440,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 440,
        "endChar": 29
