      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, after several attempts here I can\u0027t seem to find a way to check CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP at build time without giving config.h an include for our Rp definitions or removing the default pullup from config.h.\n\nI did add a follow-up to clarify that setting 0 turns off our source-out port balancing. \n\nExample failure if we put a check in the DPM code comparing CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP:\n\nIn file included from include/common.h:238,\n                 from include/charge_state.h:8,\n                 from common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c:11:\ninclude/config.h:4722:30: error: \"TYPEC_RP_1A5\" is not defined, evaluates to 0 [-Werror\u003dundef]\n #define CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP TYPEC_RP_1A5\n                              ^~~~~~~~~~~~\ncommon/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c:377:38: note: in expansion of macro \u0027CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP\u0027\n #if (CONFIG_USB_PD_3A_PORTS \u003e 0) \u0026\u0026 (CONFIG_USB_PD_PULLUP \u003d\u003d TYPEC_RP_3A0)",
